 chaperones  from the egyptian ministry of  antiquities and having visited this site  personally i have to say that it appears  that something devastating happened to  this ancient temple as well  and keep in mind that the condition in  which we see it today is after many  centuries of its stone having been  removed from the site to be recycled and  reused on other structures in the area  and by the way  that is the explanation as to why the  site was destroyed in the first place to  reuse the stone  however i would argue that stone  recycling does not explain the full  nature of the devastated remnants of  this site  like i always say look and think for  yourself it seems to me that there is  more to the story of abuser and i have  to say that i am very curious as to why  this site is so shielded from the  general public to the point that you  have to pay thousands of dollars to get  special government permission to even  see it with your own eyes now there are  other sites around egypt that appear to  have been obliterated by a catastrophe  as well but what i want to show you now  are sites ancient sites all the way over  in south america that appear to have  been destroyed  in my previous video i shared and  discussed the perplexing mystery of  involving 80 ton stones that were  somehow brought a mile down a mountain  from the quarry immediately carried  across a river  transported through a valley and then  brought to the top of a steep  mountainous hill in the peruvian andes  to the ancient inca site that is called  oyante tombo if you haven't watched that  video definitely check it out after this  one as you will clearly see that  something devastating happened here as  well  as at the top of this incredible site  there are massive monolithic stone  blocks that totally stand out from the  multiple other types of stonework found  in the area at least three different  construction methods in fact which is  interesting when you consider that the  historical experts claim that this had  to have been created by the same  civilization and at the same time  but i have to say that i highly doubt  that but that aside notice how the  largest and most impressive pieces of  stone are scattered about many of which  are broken and clearly what's left over  of whatever this site was prior to its  obvious destruction yet it is claimed  that the site simply wasn't completed  they do not say it was destroyed they  say the inca just did not finish it  yeah i'm not so sure about that either  especially when you consider that at the  bottom of this mountain are the remnants  of various broken pieces of stonework  that appear to have tumbled down the  mountain long ago  and this really shouldn't be a surprise  when we consider that the andes  mountains are already known for their  powerful earthquakes that have taken  place over the millennia but earthquake  or not clearly something catastrophic  happened here but then there's the  lesser-known peruvian site of sioustani  located along lake titicaca not far from  the bolivian border  this is one of those places that  pictures simply do not do justice  the ultra ride camera lenses that are  necessary to capture the full size of  these impressive stone work also distort  the true depth of these behemoth which  with your own eyes when seen in person  is totally different  this will be a topic for another video  but right now let's focus on the obvious  destruction at this site  and although this will sound crazy it  literally appears to have been exploded  notice how these massive multi-ton stone  blocks are scattered everywhere  this is not a matter of these ruins  being deconstructed over the centuries  and stone blocks being moved around  no when you visit this site you would be  amazed to see that these massive blocks  are scattered and broken as if they were  thrown hundreds of feet into the air and  falling all around the area perhaps the  best example is what you're seeing here  these stones are at least 10 tons and if  they were carried and set down that  would not explain that the fact they are  cracked in half but pictures never do it  justice so observe this short video that  i filmed while visiting this site last  august and forgive the shaky camera and  quick panning but it paints you a  picture for what the environment looks  like surrounding the area  again look and think for yourself  does this really appear to have been  deconstructed with the stones casually  just dropped about the area some of  which by the way are a couple hundred  yards away and here's another question  to think about  why would they deconstruct it only to  rebuild with significantly smaller and  less  precise stones  i said it before and i'm saying it again  clearly there is more to the story about  these ancient sites than what's been  theorized by people in modern times many  of which have never even visited these  places in person make no mistake it is  indeed a true mystery and that is the  point of this video that there are  significant ancient sites around the  world including even a lost capital of  ancient egypt where something  unbelievably destructive happened to and  yet somehow  so few people are even aware of and i  have to say i find that fascinating  because the question becomes  what on earth happened to these sites  was it some type of massive flooding or  tsunami event or perhaps some type of  cosmic air burst in the atmosphere from  an exploded asteroid  the option there are many options so  definitely leave a comment and share  what your thoughts and insight is on  this because it will make this already  thought-provoking topic that much more  interesting but that said i'll close it  up here because this will set the stage  for other videos that i'm currently  working on  but i'm jimmy corsetti my channel is  called bright insight hit the like  button and subscribe and i have many  more interesting videos to come real  soon  take care everybody
 

